{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RHLW-2026-1e5a12126876a6e2","published":"2026-11-18T14:43:25Z","modified":"2026-11-18T23:14:00.220132955Z","upstream":["CVE-2023-34149","CVE-2023-34396","CVE-2023-50164","CVE-2024-53677","CVE-2025-64775","CVE-2025-66675","CVE-2026-104711","CVE-2026-104712","CVE-2026-104714","CVE-2026-73634","CVE-2026-73635","GHSA-2j39-qcjm-428w","GHSA-43mq-6xmg-29vm","GHSA-4g42-gqrg-4633","GHSA-8f6x-v685-g2xc","GHSA-rg58-xhh7-mqjw","GHSA-xx7v-hqxh-cjr9"],"summary":"Lightwell Security Advisory: struts2-core 6.1.1.rhlw-00021","details":"Red Hat Lightwell has released org.apache.struts:struts2-core 6.1.1.rhlw-00021 with backported fixes for CVE-2023-34149, CVE-2023-34396, CVE-2023-50164, CVE-2024-53677, CVE-2025-64775, CVE-2025-66675, CVE-2026-104711, CVE-2026-104712, CVE-2026-104714, CVE-2026-73634, and CVE-2026-73635.\n\nCVE-2023-34149: Apache Struts: DoS via OOM owing to not properly checking of list bounds\n\nCVE-2023-34396: Apache Struts: DoS via OOM owing to no sanity limit on normal form fields in multipart forms\n\nCVE-2023-50164: Apache Struts: File upload component had a directory traversal vulnerability\n\nCVE-2024-53677: Apache Struts: Mixing setters for uploaded files and normal fields can allow bypass file upload checks\n\nCVE-2025-64775: Apache Struts: File leak in multipart request processing causes disk exhaustion (DoS)\n\nCVE-2025-66675: Apache Struts: File leak in multipart request processing causes disk exhaustion (DoS) - version ranges fixed\n\nCVE-2026-104711: Apache Struts: OGNL injection in the legacy RESTful action mapper\n\nCVE-2026-104712: Apache Struts: Disproportionate response size when rendering BigDecimal request parameters\n\nCVE-2026-104714: Apache Struts: Shared message formatter exposes date and time values across concurrent requests\n\nCVE-2026-73634: Apache Struts: Unbounded read of a Content Security Policy violation report\n\nCVE-2026-73635: Apache Struts: Unbounded growth of localized-text caches driven by the request locale\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for org.apache.struts:struts2-core 6.1.1 from Maven Central.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"org.apache.struts:struts2-core","ecosystem":"Red Hat Lightwell:Maven","purl":"pkg:maven/org.apache.struts/struts2-core"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6.1.1.rhlw-00021"}]}],"versions":["2.0.11","2.0.11.1","2.0.11.2","2.0.12","2.0.14","2.0.5","2.0.6","2.0.8","2.0.9","2.1.2","2.1.6","2.1.8","2.1.8.1","2.2.1","2.2.1.1","2.2.3","2.2.3.1","2.3.1","2.3.1.1","2.3.1.2","2.3.12","2.3.14","2.3.14.1","2.3.14.2","2.3.14.3","2.3.15","2.3.15.1","2.3.15.2","2.3.15.3","2.3.16","2.3.16.1","2.3.16.2","2.3.16.3","2.3.20","2.3.20.1","2.3.20.3","2.3.24","2.3.24.1","2.3.24.3","2.3.28","2.3.28.1","2.3.29","2.3.3","2.3.30","2.3.31","2.3.32","2.3.33","2.3.34","2.3.35","2.3.36","2.3.37","2.3.4","2.3.4.1","2.3.7","2.3.8","2.5","2.5-BETA1","2.5-BETA2","2.5-BETA3","2.5.1","2.5.10","2.5.10.1","2.5.12","2.5.13","2.5.14","2.5.14.1","2.5.16","2.5.17","2.5.18","2.5.2","2.5.20","2.5.22","2.5.25","2.5.26","2.5.27","2.5.28","2.5.28.1","2.5.28.2","2.5.28.3","2.5.29","2.5.30","2.5.31","2.5.32","2.5.33","2.5.5","2.5.8","6.0.0","6.0.3","6.1.1"],"database_specific":{"lightwell":{"backport_base_version":"6.1.1","remediated_version":"6.1.1.rhlw-00021","repository_url":"https://packages.redhat.com/lightwell/java/remediated/"},"source":"https://github.com/project-lightwell/lightwell-osv/blob/main/advisories/RHLW-2026-1e5a12126876a6e2.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/WW/S2-063"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2023/34xxx/CVE-2023-34149.json"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-34149"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8f6x-v685-g2xc"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/WW/S2-064"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://github